<title>SINGAPORE: Thai oil to restart 35,000-bpd unit this weekend.</title>
<headline>Thai oil to restart 35,000-bpd unit this weekend.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refiner Thai Oil plans to restart this weekend a 35,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) crude unit following a scheduled three-week maintenance, a company official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The unit was originally scheduled to start-up on September 25 following a shutdown on September 3, a source close to the company said.</p>
<p>The crude unit is located at Thai Oil's 220,000 bpd refinery at Sri Racha on Thailand's eastern seaboard.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
